  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="transcription" xml:id="transcription_aad_0136" xml:lang="en">
        <div type="letter">
        <pb facs="https://iiif.acdh.oeaw.ac.at/aad/aad_00443/" ed="1r" type="sheet"/>
          <opener>
            <lb/>Mr.<dateline><rs type="place" ref="#amp_place_id_1">Vienna</rs>, <date>28 March 1966</date></dateline>
            <persName>
              <lb/><rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_1">W.H.Auden</rs>
            </persName>
            <placeName>
              <lb/><rs type="place" ref="#amp_place_id_2">Hinterholz 5
              <lb/>Kirchstetten
              <lb/>Niederösterreich</rs>
            </placeName>
            <salute>
              <lb/>Dear Sir,
            </salute>
        </opener>
          <p>
            <lb/><space quantity="5" unit="char"/>Last year the "<rs>Österreichische Gesellschaft für Literatur</rs>"
            <lb/>arranged two International Round-Table Conferences to discuss
            <lb/>"The theatre of today and today in the theatre" and "The novel
            <lb/>in the present century". Both were attended by some of the lead-
            <lb/>ing writers and crities of the day, and the world-wide interest
            <lb/>evidenced by the long extracts from the discussions in newspapers,
            <lb/>literary periodicals, and radio and TV reports has led us to plan
            <lb/>a further Conference next autumn to discuss "Literature: tradi-
            <lb/>tion and revolution". A feature of the Conference, as in the case
            <lb/>of last year's, will be the presence of leading authorities from
            <lb/>both East and West.
          </p>
          <p>
            <lb/><space quantity="5" unit="char"/>The Conference will be from 23-25 October 1966 in <rs type="place" ref="#amp_place_id_1">Vienna</rs>,
            <lb/>the three mornings being set aside for discussions in the
            <lb/>presence of an invited audience of journalists and critics. The
            <lb/>languages of the Conference will be English, French and German.
            <lb/>As last year, a number of journalists <subst><del rend="erased" hand="#type_cc_kraus"><unclear></unclear></del><add place="superimposed" hand="#hand_black_kraus">from</add></subst> both East and West
            <lb/>will come to <rs type="place" ref="#amp_place_id_1">Vienna</rs> with the special purpose of reporting on
            <lb/>this Conference. On the third evening all those taking part in
            <lb/>the Conference will foregather in the Redoutensaal of the <rs type="place" ref="#amp_place_id_89">Hofburg</rs>
            <lb/>for a meeting, open to the public, at which the results of the
            <lb/>Conference will be summarised.
        </p>
        <p>
          <lb/><space quantity="5" unit="char"/>May we have the pleasure of inviting you to this Conference?
          <lb/>We are confident that anything you have to say will be much
          <lb/>appreciated by all present. You will shortly be sent further
          <lb/>details; but meanwhile it would greatly assist us if you would
          <lb/>let us know whether you can accept our invitation or not. We are
          <lb/>glad to be able to offer you a compensation of S 3.000, and we
          <lb/>shall of course be responsible for your air ticket and your
          <lb/>hotel accommodation, <add place="end" hand="#type_kraus">in case you should not be in Austria.</add>
        </p>
        <closer>
          <salute>
            <lb/><space quantity="5" unit="char"/>Hoping to receive your acceptance in dug course,
          </salute>
          <salute>
            <lb/><space quantity="21" unit="char"/>I remain with cordial greetings,
          </salute>
          <salute>
            <lb/><space quantity="41" unit="char"/>I remain with cordial greetings,
          </salute>
          <signed>
            <lb/><space quantity="38" unit="char"/><rs>Dr. Wolfgang Kraus</rs>
          </signed>
          <lb/>Invitations have been sent to
          <lb/>(See encl.)
        </closer>
        <pb facs="https://iiif.acdh.oeaw.ac.at/aad/aad_00444/" ed="1v" type="sheet"/>
      </div>
      </div>
    </body>
